Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mwifiex: sdio: add opt-in legacy scan parameter

The Surface RT's Windows SD8797 combo firmware 14.62.17.p215 initializes
Bluetooth over UART but rejects HostCmd_CMD_802_11_SCAN_EXT (0x107).
NetworkManager gets no scan results. The SD8797 device table enables extended
scanning regardless of which firmware image is loaded.

Add a read-only force_legacy_scan module parameter so a controlled trial can
use the existing legacy scan command and matching request/response paths.
Default behavior is unchanged. This is an experimental compatibility switch,
not a claim that the older firmware supports every other driver command.

Enable before probe with options mwifiex_sdio force_legacy_scan=1, or with
mwifiex_sdio.force_legacy_scan=1 on the kernel command line.

---

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/sdio.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/sdio.c
@@ -19,6 +19,10 @@
 
 #define SDIO_VERSION	"1.0"
 
+static bool force_legacy_scan;
+module_param(force_legacy_scan, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(force_legacy_scan, "Use legacy scanning (default: false)");
+
 static void mwifiex_sdio_work(struct work_struct *work);
 
 static const struct mwifiex_if_ops sdio_ops;
@@ -2615,7 +2619,10 @@
 	}
 
 	adapter->auto_tdls = card->can_auto_tdls;
-	adapter->ext_scan = card->can_ext_scan;
+	adapter->ext_scan = card->can_ext_scan && !force_legacy_scan;
+	if (force_legacy_scan && card->can_ext_scan)
+		mwifiex_dbg(adapter, MSG,
+			    "extended scan disabled by force_legacy_scan\n");
 	return 0;
 }
 
